{"version":1,"key":"card:638","content":{"id":638,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"48355200-8265-45e9-a88e-79ceaa6e2719","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"读了一篇文章，"},{"type":"link","url":"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/PJF5d7fvnQmUsClnBBTteA","openEdit":false,"tauContract":"ebf1d56e356279ad64279a16e90d9b28280f70eac20d5071950fc0c4b5c364a6","collabId":"a065f5e3-531c-425a-a0ff-a1e5c4deb24d","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"张朝阳随口而说的这几段话，就是最顶级的学习方法指南！"}]},{"type":"formatted","text":"其中关于碎片化学习和系统性学习的阐述有一些感触："}]},{"type":"bulleted-list","tauContract":"b74d37e5bfbf2503c151b31f93763a8fb42e80426564246cbb0af72201a60e8c","collabId":"7af2af83-9522-45da-b763-ae7656999d22","children":[{"type":"list-item","tauContract":"fe3a1fc1f6dcf1c1c317754db368a19bd85cab343431da98cae17d783eaa1c02","collabId":"8dfd8fbd-77a7-47df-9536-fdd5a0ae4f8c","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"db7d61ad-bfbe-4ff6-b8d4-04fdfd099e6d","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"人脑是反系统的，人脑就是碎片化的"}]}]},{"type":"list-item","tauContract":"fe3a1fc1f6dcf1c1c317754db368a19bd85cab343431da98cae17d783eaa1c02","collabId":"a8bb8612-4fbc-439d-b342-36d4c959b368","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"40f62b77-abc2-453c-bb8c-bb56be9731ec","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"人脑的高效的学习策略是"},{"type":"formatted","bold":true,"text":"学习时我们要让大脑始终保持在最兴奋的状态"},{"type":"formatted","text":"，而系统学习太枯燥了，大部分情况下无法引发思考，只是在被动的接收信息，无法内化为知识，你以为系统学习了，实际了很快就忘掉了"}]}]},{"type":"list-item","tauContract":"fe3a1fc1f6dcf1c1c317754db368a19bd85cab343431da98cae17d783eaa1c02","collabId":"4d47fe2a-2cf0-4373-9911-93f3a91bd1c0","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"21390e9e-a74a-4418-ba19-f46415218557","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"大部分的时间要花在思考上，小部分的时间花在接收知识上，平时多想问题，想到一个地方不知道，这个时候去查一下，然后回到思考"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"bc895747-5df3-496d-aa9b-4439a6fa75c0","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"这个和我的感悟比较像，我们想快速了解一个领域，系统学习的效率不是最好的，最好的办法就是直接就扎进去这个领域，在这个领域摸爬滚打，遇山开山，遇水搭桥，遇到问题去解决问题，而不是先系统学习，把所有的坑趟完（这也不可能），然后才肯进入这个领域，平白给自己设立门槛。"}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"985b998f-da16-4ccd-99b1-3909a74d9a02","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"但是我以往平日的做法又不是这样，我的做法却又偏向于系统学习，主要的学习途径就是看书，而不是去思考当前遇到的问题，然后去解决这些问题，所以我的学习效率就偏低，而且读了这么多书却没有启发什么思考，也给自己平添焦虑。所以这也引发了我对这种学习方式的反思，"},{"type":"content-link","contentId":444,"contentType":"card","contentTitle":"","refId":526,"tauContract":"720a42c66441f65bfc897253311b73deb687a68a60da46dffe8c7b8537a65760","collabId":"c85b4a6d-2581-4b7a-8ea0-5c8c6dca46d8","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"我最近做的一些事情却下意识的和碎片化学习相符"}]},{"type":"formatted","text":"，"},{"type":"formatted","bold":true,"color":"#245bdb","darkColor":"#70a0ff","text":"我不在强行的要求自己读书记笔记或者引发思考（当然如果当时有好的想法也会记下来），而是把书本或者看的视频等材料当做是一个问题或想法收集器，我把看到的不懂的概念，不明白的流程，感兴趣的议题全部记录下来，并转化为一个个的问题，我现在的学习方式就是去解决这些问题，在解决这些问题的时候，会引发我的思考，并且会促使我从各种渠道去搜集相关信息，相比于记录读书笔记要广泛且深刻的多。"}]},{"type":"image","url":"http://blog-hostimaging.oss-cn-beijing.aliyuncs.com/image_951f27da-3219-48a8-a499-96fde466b06c.webp","uuid":"acec1040-6ac9-4152-b6c4-3b5d2466b63d","pasteUploading":false,"previewUrl":"http://blog-hostimaging.oss-cn-beijing.aliyuncs.com/image_951f27da-3219-48a8-a499-96fde466b06c.webp","width":760,"tauContract":"9d766f08643a09b151c9500b642decb7d9f8625878621cbd90af820668058ac0","collabId":"2426a9d6-e938-4e42-a417-e379aa0ac60b","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":""}]}],"tags":["个人成长","思考"],"createTime":1762834169042,"updateTime":1763047618774,"linkedCards":[]},"meta":{"type":"card","publishTime":1763047618774},"links":{"card:526":{"key":"card:526","type":"card","id":526}}}